      "cancel": [],
      "conversion": "@Redirect of level.getEntitiesOfClass(LivingEntity.class, box) in HealEvents.onLivingHeal (the event captured from the handler's argument): on a ServerLevel (exact class) whose player list holds no player whose use item is the Dungeon Shield, or when the healed entity is a player blocking with it, an empty list without the search; while one uses it, the same search for Player.class (the loop acts on players only: the same players in the same order), which also answers client levels, a player's tracking start in progress and a stepped-aside session; the search as shipped only with the flag off or the shield unregistered. @Redirect (require 0) of the startTracking call in Forge's PersistentEntitySectionManager.addEntityWithoutEvent: for a player the gate steps aside during it, and for good when the player is not on its level's player list afterwards or it throws; the gate also stands aside until that redirect has run once, so it stands aside when another mod redirects Forge's entity-tracking call (Mixin keeps one redirect, the one of higher priority: ours has priority 500, so another mod's at the default 1000 or above makes it skip ours with a \"@Redirect conflict\" warning, and with require 0 / expect 0 the game starts); helper bons.furious.patch.compositematerial_coo49.HealScanGate",
      "license": "MIT (Composite Material): no Composite Material code is carried; the gate repeats its one-line blocking test on the level's player list"
